{"title":"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the plane let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a circle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> a line tangent to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> a point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />.  Find the locus of all points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with the following property: there exists two points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c52aff9dd9987076c0ac4fecccf59b6ed8bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the inscribed circle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c587b0c1e5de0bde79b9d8c36913c16dee04d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ObCzaZwujGw\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ObCzaZwujGw</a> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note: This is an alternate method to what it is shown on the video.  This alternate method is too long and too intensive in solving algebraic equations.  A lot of steps have been shortened in this solution.  The solution in the video provides a much faster solution,\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius of the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We define a cartesian coordinate system in two dimensions with the circle center at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> and circle equation to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f36f3e70890ee101453336a265cf686281e47ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2}+y{2}=r^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We define the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> by the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2f41f9a5c450e150271607aecbbac9fc4ae076.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" />, with point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> at a distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> from the tangent and cartesian coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/a/0daa61b3181e8a690f481bf294364fe3dccdccf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m,-r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the distance from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that the coordinates for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/8/ae847c82ced8964634e798691605c611577f5f71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m+d,-r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" /> and thus the coordinates for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/c/2aca4f83e29fc1a09a297d5963f3657528e8c153.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m-d,-r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> be the points where lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec6916b50feec24773d374eaada26a95bcabc6fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> are tangent to circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>First we get the coordinates for points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since the circle is the incenter we know the following properties:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/c/e9cefe56d3fe3ef79e2808b138f6dcd3b81f750b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left| RU \\right| = \\left| RT \\right|=(m+d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/1/2c1ce6c012cfec7d61e79f1c80fbc6f2fb5d17b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left| QU \\right| = \\left| QS \\right|=(m-d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>Therefore, to get the coordinates of point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/291de77f478f945dda54f845c2025dd1e4a09878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T=(T_{x},T_{y})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" />, we solve the following equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8fb40e04b8f8f849831b229214ca4c3cfa0cf7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{x}^{2}+T_{y}^2=r^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"106\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/c/76c50e3fbef876d393c5f611895d027277188e8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left| RT \\right|^{2}=(m+d-T_{x})^{2}+(r+T_{y})^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"275\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/0/44059918d657d4bb29fc367fa932241f51c36477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m+d)^{2}=(m+d-T_{x})^{2}+(r+T_{y})^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"299\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>After a lot of algebra, this solves to:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/3/1d38f09c585331ec6d423a52051ffa740dcdd917.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{x}=\\frac{2r^{2}(m+d)}{(m+d)^{2}+r^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"157\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b96b0e2fe7eabcae49ce2dee4d93699158bea102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{y}=\\frac{r\\left[ (m+d)^{2}-r^{2} \\right]}{(m+d)^{2}+r^{2} }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"178\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Now we calculate the slope of the line that passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec6916b50feec24773d374eaada26a95bcabc6fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> which is perpendicular to the line that passes from the center of the circle to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> as follows:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12121fb8ae12c9c16aba1efc2d241646823849d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Slope_{PR}=\\frac{-T_{x}}{T_{y}}=\\frac{-2r(m+d)}{(m+d)^{2}-r^2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"272\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Then, the equation of the line that passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec6916b50feec24773d374eaada26a95bcabc6fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is as follows:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/d/15d131ceb7a38af36757b8eef0459ba709c8d518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Line_{PR}\\colon \\; y+r=\\frac{-2r(m+d)}{(m+d)^{2}-r^2)}\\left( x-(m+d) \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"374\" height=\"45\" /> \n</p><p>Now we get the coordinates of point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/4/874bc3e9a9859bc6f9830661bf1f5582907bdf2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=(S_{x},S_{y})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" />, we solve the following equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d540b9af4cf8ad4c91cc9793fe19a13c34ff927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{x}^{2}+S_{y}^2=r^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"104\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dbe4925adb924e0229484ffa2fd8621862b846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left| QT \\right|^{2}=(m-d-S_{x})^{2}+(r+S_{y})^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"276\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d084f4422d24e689b476e17024f441f205ec6903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m-d)^{2}=(m-d-S_{x})^{2}+(r+S_{y})^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"300\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>After a lot of algebra, this solves to:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/3/bd36b070890f1cbfbde5708cc6614419db27a0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{x}=\\frac{2r^{2}(m-d)}{(m-d)^{2}+r^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"157\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/40337bc1e901475db8a3154f3a0a54a69a150c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{y}=\\frac{r\\left[ (m-d)^{2}-r^{2} \\right]}{(m-d)^{2}+r^{2} }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"179\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Now we calculate the slope of the line that passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> which is perpendicular to the line that passes from the center of the circle to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> as follows:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/3/9637d72c303facce90bb40bea7052ae2235fabb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Slope_{PQ}=\\frac{-S_{x}}{S_{y}}=\\frac{-2r(m-d)}{(m-d)^{2}-r^2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"273\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Then, the equation of the line that passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is as follows:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d4d02f19df07b0aa3eb6fd239ec1a15749d23ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Line_{PQ}\\colon \\; y+r=\\frac{-2r(m-d)}{(m-d)^{2}-r^2)}\\left( x-(m-d) \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"375\" height=\"45\" /> \n</p><p>Now we solve for the coordinates for point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/f/fcf2d015070a78111be7d0c728e0d38ceeb1d0df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=(P_{x},P_{y})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" /> by calculating the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/2/7c2bde73d97e065ac7350852fedc52e377a713df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Line_{PR}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2a78be8baae316301fbb3b67203765eeae4b3f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Line_{PQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" /> as follows:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39c4c1a34300c0e38eadb4b995335bff15ea66e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-2r(m+d)}{(m+d)^{2}-r^2)}\\left( P_{x}-(m+d) \\right)=\\frac{-2r(m-d)}{(m-d)^{2}-r^2)}\\left( P_{x}-(m-d) \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"506\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89e5e5a22fd6b9131b9d06ac519f93151a617c85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/b/36bf65e0f0815356fde507d0d6cc8efa3662be81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{x}=\\frac{2mr^{2}}{m^{2}+r^{2}-d^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"151\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/7/427e02c2084e01e46e72d551bb60aff53cd421e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"21\" height=\"19\" /> we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/c/05c52e7d39c74a24e06198c22283c1fac6d26969.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y}=\\frac{-2r(m-d)}{(m-d)^{2}-r^2)}\\left( \\frac{2mr^{2}}{m^{2}+r^{2}-d^{2}}-(m-d) \\right)-r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"413\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77d29acc21b86015a70809599994565cb4347902.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y}=\\frac{r(m^{2}-r^{2}-d^{2})}{m^{2}+r^{2}-d^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"173\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Now we need to find the limit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89e5e5a22fd6b9131b9d06ac519f93151a617c85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/7/427e02c2084e01e46e72d551bb60aff53cd421e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"21\" height=\"19\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> approaches infinity:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/2/74251e92096eaf0703974f178737973fbaada693.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{x_{d \\to \\infty}}=\\lim_{d \\to \\infty} \\frac{2mr^{2}}{m^{2}+r^{2}-d^{2}}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"250\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6c2dd1b88258afa336e028687b654f1817ab2e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{y_{d \\to \\infty}}=\\lim_{d \\to \\infty} \\frac{r(m^{2}-r^{2}-d^{2})}{m^{2}+r^{2}-d^{2}}=r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"272\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>This means that the locus of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> starts at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/9/079c557b86ce9aa37377f45f12f94b78c6ae7426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> on the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> but that point is not included in the locus as that is the limit.\n</p><p>If we assume that the locus is a ray that starts at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/9/079c557b86ce9aa37377f45f12f94b78c6ae7426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> let's calculate the slope of such ray:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/9/7c91ea62189fd331c6653dba6ca050b3a98c445b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Slope_{locus}=\\frac{P_{y}-r}{P_{x}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"157\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/a/95a37f0b3816ae9ecbeb79c5435879532339027c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Slope_{locus}=\\frac{\\frac{r(m^{2}-r^{2}-d^{2})}{m^{2}+r^{2}-d^{2}}-r}{\\frac{2mr^{2}}{m^{2}+r^{2}-d^{2}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"223\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0acf71a4a51ae5c29fdcf65f56def23820fcbe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Slope_{locus}=\\frac{-r^{2}}{2m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"136\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Since the calculated slope of such locus at any point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is not dependent on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and solely dependent on fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, then this proves the slope is fixed and thus the locus is a ray that starts at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/9/079c557b86ce9aa37377f45f12f94b78c6ae7426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> excluding that point and with a slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c93b00412042cf05d1310605b88d9f3f908aac44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-r^{2}}{2m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"36\" height=\"41\" /> in the cartesian coordinate system moving upwards to infinity.\n</p><p>We can also write the equation of the locus as: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/a/a5a0d71cd85974456a72d09e8817e263ffa9bdf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{-r^{2}}{2m}x+r,\\;\\;\\forall y&gt;r\\;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"186\" height=\"41\" />and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6ee81a7a535d87853e848c77654cc36104a75e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>~Tomas Diaz. orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We give a synthetic solution to this problem. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the tangency point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/3/b239e47c75fa1adfb0e7d7fb6bf219fcc53f86d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&#39;$\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> be the reflections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. We claim that the locus is the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/a/c8ad38a68c84c51d4e6212ce163ca1b9818ff264.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&#39;X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c587b0c1e5de0bde79b9d8c36913c16dee04d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> be a triangle with the given properties. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the tangency point of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />-excircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c587b0c1e5de0bde79b9d8c36913c16dee04d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />, so by homothety at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/3/b239e47c75fa1adfb0e7d7fb6bf219fcc53f86d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&#39;$\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear. \n</p><p>Conversely, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d41a67c2c8d44c8c1501a03223484f2965069d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q\\ne R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> be two points on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec6916b50feec24773d374eaada26a95bcabc6fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> are tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. A homothety at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> sending <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/3/b239e47c75fa1adfb0e7d7fb6bf219fcc53f86d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&#39;$\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> sends <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />-excircle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/d/74dd5ad800ea081237b0f8448a2aed47d49ea475.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QD=RX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c52aff9dd9987076c0ac4fecccf59b6ed8bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>~Alexander Chew. alexanderchew2021@gmail.com\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO\" title=\"1992 IMO\">1992 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1992 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183429\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.046 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 668/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1238/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 22431/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.803      1 -total\n 53.64%    6.331      1 Template:IMO_box\n 45.19%    5.334      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25417:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017183429 and revision id 255115. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}